{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/279286-prematurely-cut-game","id":279286,"title":"Prematurely Cut Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-12T18:44:46-07:00","id":279286,"title":"Prematurely Cut Game","content":"So I suppose this is more musing/complaining more than anything else, but input is always welcome.<br /> <br /> So I was running a Scion game with these people: new group, cool people for the most part. Scion's got its problems, to be sure, but we were house-ruling it and suchforth and people <i>seemed</i> to be having fun. There were a few minor criticisms, which maybe I should have done more to address, but they didn't seem particularly crucial, just &quot;maybe think about X&quot; type. They even requested we increase the frequency of games from once a month to once every two weeks, which I thought was a particularly promising sign. I mean, I wouldn't request an increase of frequency of something I'm not enjoying.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the game was drawing to a close, I'd just given them their next major plot hook because they'd indicated that they felt a bit lost without some direction, and completing this next bit would put a cap on the story. I mentioned this, and that I saw it ending in 2 - 4 sessions or so, which they seemed OK with.<br /> <br /> Next thing I know, I get a message from one of them (who for sake of ease we shall call Simon), saying that he'd spoken to the others and that they were feeling bored with the game, and wanted to end it prematurely. When pressed, he cited a few of the criticisms mentioned previously, including, oddly enough, the lack of direction. Well, I can't really force people to play in a game if they're not enjoying it, and further prodding didn't really elicit more information, so I bowed back, and the group starting their next game - a D:tD game, run by Simon, oddly enough.<br /> <br /> It honestly really surprised me, and frankly it kind of has shaken my confidence. I always thought I was a pretty good ST: not perfect, by any measure, I do tend to let the players drive the action rather than setting up goalposts, which can lead to things being a bit undirected, and I do tend to be maybe more permissive than I strictly should (never had criticisms about that part, though). But players always seemed to have fun. But ending a game prematurely in favour of another one which could have easily waited? That's not a good sign. I myself have only ever bowed out of one game due to quality, and that was far and away the worst game I have ever seen or heard of. So, the implication that I'm even remotely that bad? Not only does it shake my confidence in how I was running that game - I could take that, we all run a dud sometimes - but in my whole style. Also, since I've never detected any kind of hint of dissatisfaction on that level, it even raises questions about my ability to read people, which as a psych postgrad looking to research is kind of a serious issue.<br /> <br /> I find myself looking back at the other games and group I've run with. Similarly, they've seemed to enjoy themselves, but then I saw them seem to enjoy themselves in a game of D&amp;D that was truly terrible (not as bad as the other one, but still pretty damn awful), so clearly either they're weird or my reading's off. Granted, the dynamic of that group was seriously messed up, but still.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, oddly enough, it's not looking like I'm going to have the opportunity to run for a while, but frankly, I'm wondering if I <i>should</i> be running, if I'm that blind. I mean, I never pretended I was telling any profound stories, or emotionally moving my players, but I've always thought they were fun, at least.<br /> <br /> That said, the game being run by Simon is pretty...different. He's made some odd decisions: throwing out the Beats system (fair enough, but really something that should have been discussed, or at least mentioned before the end of the second session), lingering on some parts which in my opinion would be better left undefined. and entities that we have no chance of defeating or really affecting worth a damn.<br /> <br /> So is it maybe just a group-style difference? Or have I really held the wrong end of the stick of ST-ing for all these years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T19:25:14-07:00","id":279303,"title":"","content":"I live in a constant state of second-guessing myself and the amount of fun my group is having. We're Midwesterners, so we're genetically predisposed toward passive-aggressiveness in the first place; and we're gamers, so most of us are unassertive, timid, and unwilling to criticize a person except behind his back. What you're describing does not seem like an unusual phenomenon at all, but does it mean you shouldn't be running games? Eh. Maybe not for that group, but that group is not all games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T23:02:22-07:00","id":279393,"title":"","content":"Sure, but there's a difference between general second-guessing and nagging self-doubt, which I maintain keeps you sharp, and having a game cancelled on you.<br /> <br /> Never even heard of that happening...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 10-13-2014, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T02:20:27-07:00","id":279462,"title":"","content":"It certainly is weird... I can't advice you much because I've been running with the same group for over 10 years. We're not just players but great friends, therefore my interactions with other players are very limited. Everyone, apart from myself, is a great ST. Sure each has his personal style, his strong and weak points, but in general they are amazing at their respective games (each one has a favourite game to ST). <br /> <br /> Despite all this, no one is perfect. And if one is STing and things go sour, we talk to him, in group or in private, telling what we liked, what we didn't and through the years we've grown as players and STs adapting and improving the game.<br /> <br /> I've heard many weird stories, the old foruns had a Thread to complaint about you ST and another to complaint about your Players (we actually should revive that, had a lot of laughs), but players just quitting? And after asking to increase the gaming sessions? I'd react like you did: clueless. It makes no sense at all.<br /> <br /> Besides, don't second guess your gaming because it had nothing to do with why they left:<br /> <br /> 1st - They talked with each other excluding yourself;<br /> 2nd - They just announced the decision and did not present it to discussion;<br /> 3rd - They did not bring the complaints and critiques again even if it was as an ultimatum &quot;Do this or we quit.&quot;, they just quit;<br /> 4th - They immediately started another game out of the blue;<br /> <br /> This kind of behaviour tells me there's something wrong with people's education and good manners, not with the gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T09:58:20-07:00","id":279792,"title":"","content":"I've had games in that situation, where people seem to be having a good time but are not really into it all that much. A few times actually. Also been on the other side of it.<br /> <br /> What I realized is that it was often not a question of the GM skill, but just that they thought game would be like X and it ended up being like Y and they didn't find it particularly appealing, be it for mechanics, tone of the game or just overall genre, but those things are rather difficult it articulate.<br /> <br /> And it's often a variable, personal or even seasonal thing. I've found with my current players for example, I can't run a dark broody game (vampire focusing on the dark side of stuff) during the summer. It will invariably be too high energy because the players are high energy and it turns into a zany vampire adventure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}